'''Iz the Dancer''' is a [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] event. She was added in [[Version 11.1 Update|Version 11.1]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 641
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Iz the Dancer
|name2 = Iz the Alluring Dancer
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Iz the Alluring Dancer''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
A slightly awkward unit, Iz takes the role of a [[Classification|midrange rusher]] with massive damage to all traits. Though she has low base DPS for an Uber Rare, a strengthened Iz can deal damage comparable to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] when facing traited enemies. This, combined with a meager 46-second recharge time, makes Iz the Alluring Dancer one of the strongest rushers in the game in terms of raw stats.

Her role, however, is not quite the same as A. Bahamut and similar units. Instead, somewhat like [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dom Cat]], she specializes in attacking continuously to quickly defeat or knockback enemies, thus relieving the pressure on the frontline, instead of specializing in quickly defeating targets. She is thus excellent against hordes of small and medium enemies, but also against tanky backliners who mainly rely on health and range, such as [[Elder Sloth]], [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[Daboo of the Dead]], as she is quite hard to knock back.

Versatility is what she lacks, however, as it usually doesn't take much to put her life on the line, making her heavily reliant on outranging enemies and not being sniped between attacks. Luckily, her Omni Strike offers a solution, allowing her to deliver somewhat consistent damage even when heavy meatshielding prevents enemies from coming in her range after the first hit of her attack.

{{Job|Classification = Midranger & Rusher}}

